WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.188 --> 00:00:01.384
- This is gonna' get weird.

00:00:01.384 --> 00:00:04.884
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:12.976
- I love Bob Ross.

00:00:12.976 --> 00:00:16.020
He's like "Do it this way if you like to.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.909
"If it looks different
from mine, it's okay."

00:00:17.909 --> 00:00:19.210
- There's something so hypnotizing

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:22.036
about the way he speaks,
and it's just so soothing.

00:00:22.036 --> 00:00:24.039
- I know he's a painter, but I totally

00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:26.220
had no idea that he was dead.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.379
I thought he had a new Netflix show, so.

00:00:28.379 --> 00:00:29.368
- Let's do this.

00:00:29.368 --> 00:00:31.703
- Let's go right in here,

00:00:31.703 --> 00:00:33.769
and just put in a happy little glow.

00:00:33.769 --> 00:00:35.696
- So I'm painting like,
it looks like a sunset.

00:00:35.696 --> 00:00:37.503
I think I did mine
darker than his, though.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:39.238
- Kay, hold on, Bob,
give me a second here.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:40.795
- So he does move quickly.

00:00:40.795 --> 00:00:42.418
- Eh, fine, sure, yep.

00:00:42.418 --> 00:00:45.262
- Wants it to blend now, and
I don't feel good about this.

00:00:45.262 --> 00:00:46.210
- This is lookin' good!

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.842
I legitimately feel like
I'm doing a good job.

00:00:48.842 --> 00:00:50.796
- Bob, Shit, Oh God.

00:00:50.796 --> 00:00:52.228
- (muttering) Dammit, what, suck it.

00:00:52.228 --> 00:00:54.089
- I'm using the wrong brush, shit!

00:00:54.089 --> 00:00:55.889
- All we're doing is applying some very,

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.438
very basic little shapes.

00:00:57.438 --> 00:00:58.986
Think about the shape of a tree.

00:00:58.986 --> 00:01:00.739
- I'll think about the shape of a tree.

00:01:00.739 --> 00:01:03.119
Oh God, oh God. (laughs)

00:01:03.119 --> 00:01:04.586
- Well that one kinda' looks like a tree.

00:01:04.586 --> 00:01:05.730
I feel good about that.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:08.023
- Blending, we're
blending, we're blending.

00:01:08.023 --> 00:01:09.290
- I think we're using the same brush,

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:10.480
but for whatever reason,

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.063
what I'm doing is not what he's doing.

00:01:12.063 --> 00:01:13.655
- Trees look a little bit like penises,

00:01:13.655 --> 00:01:15.151
but you know what, what are you gonna' do?

00:01:15.151 --> 00:01:16.109
(growls)

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.665
- The left side looks
better than the right side.

00:01:17.665 --> 00:01:20.412
This looks like trees,
this still looks crazy.

00:01:20.412 --> 00:01:23.186
- And here, maybe, lives
a happy little bush.

00:01:23.186 --> 00:01:25.379
This is what keeps the little
rabbit warm in the winter.

00:01:25.379 --> 00:01:27.619
- It keeps a rabbit warm in the winter.

00:01:27.619 --> 00:01:30.157
Ugh, heartfelt, this scene
is not just a painting.

00:01:30.157 --> 00:01:31.723
There's life in it!

00:01:31.723 --> 00:01:33.109
- I think this is salvageable if

00:01:33.109 --> 00:01:34.936
I just stick to the lower half.

00:01:34.936 --> 00:01:38.005
- Bob's voice is what I
imagine like, if Mufasa,

00:01:38.005 --> 00:01:42.874
Morgan Freeman, and God decided
to teach a painting class.

00:01:42.874 --> 00:01:44.565
(tapping loudly)

00:01:44.565 --> 00:01:46.716
- I think these are supposed to be bushes.

00:01:46.716 --> 00:01:48.255
I can't be sure anymore.

00:01:48.255 --> 00:01:49.344
(sighs loudly)

00:01:49.344 --> 00:01:52.026
- If Bob and like the Reading Rainbow guy,

00:01:52.026 --> 00:01:53.315
did they ever team up?

00:01:53.315 --> 00:01:55.706
Because them together, like if Bob

00:01:55.706 --> 00:01:56.744
and the Reading Rainbow guy,

00:01:56.744 --> 00:01:59.698
I can't, I think his
name's LaVerne, a duo.

00:01:59.698 --> 00:02:00.726
It's not LaVerne?

00:02:00.726 --> 00:02:01.734
- Okay, so now we're basically making

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:04.487
the whole ground with
this nice blue, which,

00:02:04.487 --> 00:02:07.870
I'm finally getting the knack
of not having too much paint.

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:10.076
- I guess Guy Fieri is
kinda' the Bob Ross of food,

00:02:10.076 --> 00:02:11.912
just way less likable.

00:02:11.912 --> 00:02:13.530
Was that kinda' mean to say, sorry.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.455
Shit, what, what, what?

00:02:15.455 --> 00:02:16.672
- My confidence is back down.

00:02:16.672 --> 00:02:18.650
I felt great, and now I'm like, "Oh, Crap.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:19.666
"Mine doesn't look like that."

00:02:19.666 --> 00:02:21.197
- Maybe today we'll have a big old cabin.

00:02:21.197 --> 00:02:23.905
- Cabins, I was always
amazed by his cabins,

00:02:23.905 --> 00:02:25.142
because like, "What?"

00:02:25.142 --> 00:02:26.574
He's like, "Three strokes, and

00:02:26.574 --> 00:02:28.320
"there you have it, a beautiful cabin."

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.524
- Touching and pushing at the same time.

00:02:30.524 --> 00:02:32.808
- Can we paint it something
cooler, like a bear?

00:02:32.808 --> 00:02:34.884
- Oh God, I don't know how to do this.

00:02:34.884 --> 00:02:37.776
- I can't even imagine like,
if you're watching this IRL,

00:02:37.776 --> 00:02:39.967
commercial television, you can't pause.

00:02:39.967 --> 00:02:40.911
Who did this?

00:02:40.911 --> 00:02:42.530
- Oh, yes.

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:45.383
- I just like the sound
of this. (scraping)

00:02:45.383 --> 00:02:47.048
- The knife is always my favorite part,

00:02:47.048 --> 00:02:49.495
because he works some fuckin'
magic with this thing.

00:02:49.495 --> 00:02:53.007
- Okay, so it's like a Christmas
getaway for me and Bob.

00:02:53.007 --> 00:02:55.722
The economy's bad, so
no gifts this year, Bob.

00:02:55.722 --> 00:02:57.325
- I'm just not even
gonna' try the windows,

00:02:57.325 --> 00:02:59.088
'cuz it's clearly gonna' be a hot mess.

00:02:59.088 --> 00:03:02.221
- Um, I'm not feeling great,
this feels a little bit crazy.

00:03:02.221 --> 00:03:04.853
He's crazy, everyone's crazy,

00:03:04.853 --> 00:03:06.535
I'm crazy for thinking I could do this.

00:03:06.535 --> 00:03:08.416
- I think we'll call that
one finished, in fact.

00:03:08.416 --> 00:03:09.395
- Wait, we're done?

00:03:09.395 --> 00:03:10.918
What? (laughs)

00:03:10.918 --> 00:03:12.696
- Thank you Bob, I'll see you next time.

00:03:12.696 --> 00:03:15.093
Um, okay. (laughs)

00:03:15.093 --> 00:03:15.926
- Yeah, I think I'm done.

00:03:15.926 --> 00:03:18.843
(orchestral music)

00:03:21.992 --> 00:03:24.544
- I had to pause multiple times,

00:03:24.544 --> 00:03:27.292
and mine looks like complete
garbage after like an hour.

00:03:27.292 --> 00:03:28.298
My trees are definitely gonna' need

00:03:28.298 --> 00:03:30.891
some therapy before they're happy trees.

00:03:30.891 --> 00:03:33.001
- I am most proud of my
tree here on the right.

00:03:33.001 --> 00:03:34.664
It looks like it's ready for Christmas.

00:03:34.664 --> 00:03:36.023
He has a special place in my heart

00:03:36.023 --> 00:03:37.741
that only Bob Ross can have.

00:03:37.741 --> 00:03:41.490
I feel like I was about to
cry and I don't know why.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.290
- This looks like a
thing, like a human person

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.669
would be like, "Hmm, sure."

00:03:45.669 --> 00:03:49.024
I made this, and how
many people can say that?

00:03:49.024 --> 00:03:50.591
Thanks, Bob.

00:03:50.591 --> 00:03:52.004
- I'll see you next time.

00:03:52.004 --> 00:03:54.921
(orchestral music)

00:04:04.666 --> 00:04:05.733
(squeaking)

